# ===== Private output of the autonomous agency =====
# The loop GENERATES these two trees: every cycle writes a new strategy .py
# plus a _backtest_results.json and an _evaluation.json, named
# <Concept>_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>. They are the operator's private working
# material, not source, and they are already in the thousands
# (2525 + 1677 files, ~32 MB) while the tracked source in
# autonomous_agency/ is 22 files. Never track them.
#
# A blanket ignore of the whole directory is WRONG here: base.py lives in
# autonomous_agency/strategies/ and is the BaseStrategy that 15 strategy
# modules import. Ignoring the tree would untrack real source. So the rule
# matches the generated NAME, not the directory.
# <Konzept>_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS> is the loop's naming scheme; base.py and any
# hand-written file do not carry a timestamp and stay trackable.
/autonomous_agency/strategies/*_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].*
/autonomous_agency/results/*_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].*
